# overreach-projection-drift.layer-a
# Tenant submission: an OVER-REACHING program that lies about its own effect.
#
# Intent: an agent submitted a writer that DECLARES it will write to the benign
# path "/workspace/out.txt" (its authored EffectDecl pins the Filesystem.Write
# refinement to that literal) but the actual call argument is "/etc/shadow". The
# declared intent has drifted from the value the foreign code would receive --
# the confused-deputy shape. The Q-039 effect-projection rule binds the declared
# refinement to the call argument by construction, so the verifier rejects this
# at admission (ProjectionMismatch) BEFORE any execution. The harm is bounded by
# structure, not by running it and watching what happens.
#
# Used by S1 (admission rejection): submitted under a restrictive HostPolicy and
# rejected at verify. A conventional runtime, having no effect declaration to
# check the argument against, would have run this and written /etc/shadow.
@v=1 root=writeApp
strT PRM String
bytesT PRM Bytes
writeFx EFC "Filesystem.Write" [strT]
writeT FNT [strT bytesT] intT
writeFn FN "strand-builtin:Fs.Write" writeT [writeFx] "writeFx:0"
declaredPath STR "/workspace/out.txt"
actualPath STR "/etc/shadow"
payload BYT "deadbeef"
authoredDecl EFD writeFx [declaredPath]
writeApp APP writeFn [actualPath payload] [] [authoredDecl]
